{
 "id": "keepalive/ping-miss-restarts-clock/5m",
 "description": "The entry (20,000 tokens) expired before the ping at minute 6, so the ping read 0 and wrote it again. Turn 1 arrives at minute 9: past the TTL measured from turn 0, inside it measured from the ping. The entry gap runs from LastPing, so the phase is hot and the rescue is credited: 20,000 x ($3.75 - $0.30) = +$0.06900. The ping costs 20,000 x $3.75 + 10 x $3.00 + 1 x $15.00 = -$0.07505, so the window nets -$0.00605: a ping that missed pays for itself at the read price only.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#580",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rescue",
  "position": "beforeBStar",
  "cache": "rescue",
  "ttl": "5m",
  "lifetime": "exact",
  "keepalive": "true",
  "ping": "missed-and-wrote"
 },
 "rates": "fixture-v1",
 "open": [
  "design \u00a74.4 rule 4 takes the smaller of what the last ping READ and what the request read. A ping that missed read 0 but re-created the entry, so read literally the rescue is 0. This case credits the extent the ping covered (PingRead). The rule needs to say so",
  "design \u00a74.1 defines PingRead as the extent the ping READ, which is nil for a ping that missed; this case sets it to messages[0] so that row 2 of the phase table matches. Both need amending"
 ],
